# Module top nav tabs

Every module’s compact top tabs use `.billing-chrome` / `.billing-chrome-tab`. Copy Inventory (`src/features/inventory/InventoryLayout.tsx`). Do not invent a second tab bar.

## Compact spec (source of truth)

- Chrome: `padding: 0.35rem 0.35rem 0.35rem 0.5rem`, `border-radius: 12px`
- Tab: icon 18 / stroke 1.75 + label, `padding: 0.55rem 0.9rem`, `font-size: 0.875rem`, `border-radius: 8px`, `gap: 0.4rem`
- Active: `var(--brand)` background, white text — same for every tab
- Tab size must not change with the child page (no `:has(.sale-bill-editor)` or similar padding/font overrides)

```tsx
<div className="billing-chrome">
  <div className="billing-chrome-tabs" role="tablist">
    <NavLink role="tab" className={() => `billing-chrome-tab${selected ? ' active' : ''}`}>
      <span className="billing-chrome-tab-icon" aria-hidden>
        <Icon size={18} strokeWidth={1.75} />
      </span>
      <span className="billing-chrome-tab-label">{tab.label}</span>
    </NavLink>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Do / don't

- **Do** reuse these classes on Billing, Inventory, Reports, and any new module
- **Don't** size compact tabs from the editor/page underneath
- **Don't** give compact tabs per-type active colors
- **Exception:** Billing landing cards (`.billing-chrome--list`) keep the large colored tiles; that is not the compact tab bar
